1
00:00:00,230 --> 00:00:02,861
It's a sanctuary base! Deep-space
exploration.

2
00:00:03,458 --> 00:00:04,588
Welcome to hell. . .

3
00:00:05,262 --> 00:00:09,011
What are you lot doing here? That's
a black hole. That's impossible.

4
00:00:09,890 --> 00:00:13,149
This lump of rock is suspended
in perpetual geostationary orbit

5
00:00:13,917 --> 00:00:15,595
around that black hole,
without falling in.

6
00:00:16,889 --> 00:00:18,758
Some sort of power source is
holding us here.

7
00:00:19,539 --> 00:00:20,642
We're drilling down
to try and find it.

8
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,714
The Tardis is gone.

9
00:00:25,754 --> 00:00:28,395
Whatever it is,
it's not a natural phenomenon.

10
00:00:28,435 --> 00:00:31,033
Some form of civilisation.

11
00:00:31,073 --> 00:00:32,751
They buried something.

12
00:00:35,507 --> 00:00:38,943
What are they called? .
They're the Ood, basic slave race.

13
00:00:38,983 --> 00:00:41,541
There's something happening
with the Ood. . .

14
00:00:41,581 --> 00:00:43,839
ALL: And you will worship him.

15
00:00:47,369 --> 00:00:51,528
You can tell Toby what we've found
is civilisation.

16
00:00:51,568 --> 00:00:55,045
These are the words of the beast. . .
and he has woken.

17
00:00:55,085 --> 00:00:58,401
OOD: I have been imprisoned
for eternity.

18
00:00:58,441 --> 00:01:00,321
But no more.

19
00:01:00,361 --> 00:01:03,397
The pit is open!

20
00:01:03,437 --> 00:01:06,753
And I am free!

21
00:01:07,393 --> 00:01:10,510
"DOCTOR WHO" THEME

22
00:01:44,912 --> 00:01:46,595
Open fire!

23
00:01:53,147 --> 00:01:55,384
We're stabilising!

24
00:01:55,424 --> 00:01:57,761
We've got orbit.

25
00:02:02,136 --> 00:02:04,932
Doctor?
STATIC HISS

26
00:02:04,972 --> 00:02:08,004
Doctor, can you hear me?
Doctor, Ida, are you there?

27
00:02:09,171 --> 00:02:10,844
It's me!

28
00:02:10,884 --> 00:02:14,124
But they're coming. It's the Ood.

29
00:02:14,164 --> 00:02:15,962
They've gone mad. How many of them?

30
00:02:16,002 --> 00:02:19,676
All of them, all 50. Danny,
out of the way. Out of the way!

31
00:02:19,716 --> 00:02:22,196
But they're armed!
It's the interface device.

32
00:02:22,236 --> 00:02:25,472
I don't know how,
but they're using it as a weapon.

33
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:29,683
A-A-A-A-Aaah!

34
00:02:32,224 --> 00:02:34,158
Close Door One.

35
00:02:43,012 --> 00:02:46,249
Open Door One. Close Door One.

36
00:02:46,289 --> 00:02:48,445
Lockdown! Seal Door One!

37
00:02:48,485 --> 00:02:51,763
VOICES BABBLE

38
00:02:51,803 --> 00:02:53,481
Jefferson, what's happening?

39
00:02:53,521 --> 00:02:57,158
I've got very little ammunition,
sir, how about you?

40
00:02:57,198 --> 00:02:59,675
All I've got is a bolt-gun.

41
00:02:59,715 --> 00:03:01,952
With, uh. . .all of one bolt.

42
00:03:01,992 --> 00:03:05,908
I could take out a grand total of
one Ood, fat lot of good that is( !)

43
00:03:05,948 --> 00:03:08,866
Given the emergency,
I'd recommend. . .Strategy Nine.

44
00:03:10,066 --> 00:03:13,860
Strategy Nine, agreed. Right, we
need to get everyone together. Rose?

45
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:17,653
What about Ida and the Doctor,
any word? I can't get a reply.

46
00:03:17,693 --> 00:03:20,132
Just. . . nothing.
I keep trying, but it's. . .

47
00:03:20,172 --> 00:03:23,327
ON COMMUNICATOR:
No, sorry, I'm fine, still here!

48
00:03:23,367 --> 00:03:26,286
Oh, you could've said, you stupid. . .
FEEDBACK WHINES

49
00:03:26,326 --> 00:03:30,326
Woah. Careful. Anyway!
It's both of us, me and Ida, hello!

50
00:03:30,366 --> 00:03:32,879
But the seal opened up.

51
00:03:32,919 --> 00:03:35,237
It's gone.

52
00:03:35,277 --> 00:03:38,117
All we've got left is this. . .chasm.

53
00:03:38,157 --> 00:03:41,035
'How deep is it?' Can't tell.

54
00:03:41,075 --> 00:03:43,591
Looks like it goes down forever.
'The Pit is open. '

55
00:03:43,631 --> 00:03:49,145
That's what the voice said.
But there's nothing. . . I mean,
there's nothing coming out?

56
00:03:49,185 --> 00:03:51,822
No, no sign of the Beast.

57
00:03:51,862 --> 00:03:54,456
It said Satan.
Come on, Rose. Keep it together.

58
00:03:54,496 --> 00:03:56,674
Is there no such thing?

59
00:03:57,973 --> 00:03:59,610
Doctor.

60
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:02,888
'Doctor, tell me
there's no such thing. '

61
00:04:02,928 --> 00:04:06,566
Ida. I recommend that you
withdraw, immediately.

62
00:04:06,606 --> 00:04:11,400
But we've come all this way. . . !
OK, that was an order. Withdraw!

63
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:13,837
When that opened,
the whole planet shifted.

64
00:04:13,877 --> 00:04:17,237
One more inch, and we fall into
the black hole. This stops, now.

65
00:04:17,277 --> 00:04:20,034
But it's not much better up there,
with the Ood.

66
00:04:20,074 --> 00:04:21,831
I'm initiating Strategy Nine,

67
00:04:21,871 --> 00:04:26,052
so I need the two of you
back up top, immediately, no arg. . .

68
00:04:26,905 --> 00:04:30,061
Ida. IDA? !

69
00:04:30,101 --> 00:04:32,176
What do you think?

70
00:04:32,216 --> 00:04:34,416
He gave an order.

71
00:04:34,456 --> 00:04:37,863
Yeah, but what do YOU think?

72
00:04:40,336 --> 00:04:43,738
It said, "I am the temptation. "

73
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:49,042
If there's something in there. . .

74
00:04:49,082 --> 00:04:51,918
Why's it still hiding?

75
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:57,284
Maybe we've opened the prison,
but not the cell.

76
00:04:57,324 --> 00:05:00,211
We should go down.

77
00:05:00,251 --> 00:05:02,543
I'd go.

78
00:05:03,688 --> 00:05:08,068
What about you? Ohh, in a second.
But then again. . .

79
00:05:09,957 --> 00:05:11,955
That is so human.

80
00:05:11,995 --> 00:05:14,992
Where angels fear to tread.

81
00:05:16,074 --> 00:05:18,577
Even now, standing on the edge.

82
00:05:20,071 --> 00:05:23,145
It's that feeling you get, yeah?

83
00:05:23,185 --> 00:05:25,782
Right at the back of your head,

84
00:05:25,822 --> 00:05:28,219
that impulse,

85
00:05:28,259 --> 00:05:31,295
that strange little impulse,

86
00:05:31,335 --> 00:05:36,853
that mad little voice saying,
"Go on, go on, go on,

87
00:05:36,893 --> 00:05:39,071
"go over, go on. . . "

88
00:05:40,968 --> 00:05:43,266
Maybe it's relying on that.

89
00:05:44,362 --> 00:05:48,797
For once in my life, Officer Scott,

90
00:05:48,837 --> 00:05:51,379
I'm going to say. . .

91
00:05:52,753 --> 00:05:54,751
Retreat.

92
00:05:54,791 --> 00:05:56,831
Ohh.

93
00:05:56,871 --> 00:05:58,907
Now I know I'm getting old.

94
00:05:58,947 --> 00:06:00,504
Rose. We're coming back.

95
00:06:00,544 --> 00:06:03,065
Best news I've heard all day.

96
00:06:03,105 --> 00:06:05,781
What are you doing?

97
00:06:05,821 --> 00:06:08,939
He's infected. He brought that
thing on board - you saw it.

98
00:06:08,979 --> 00:06:14,533
Are you gonna start shooting your
own people now, is that what you're
gonna do? Is it? If necessary.

99
00:06:14,573 --> 00:06:18,299
Well, then, you'll have to shoot me.
If necessary. So what's it gonna be?

100
00:06:20,647 --> 00:06:24,081
Look at his face.
Whatever it was, it's gone.

101
00:06:24,121 --> 00:06:26,333
It passed into the Ood,
you saw it happen.

102
00:06:27,157 --> 00:06:29,614
He's clean.

103
00:06:31,195 --> 00:06:34,272
Any sign of trouble, I'll shoot him.

104
00:06:34,312 --> 00:06:37,189
You all right?

105
00:06:37,229 --> 00:06:39,907
Yeah.

106
00:06:39,947 --> 00:06:43,540
Um. Dunno. Can you remember anything?
Just. . .

107
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:45,578
It was so angry.

108
00:06:45,618 --> 00:06:50,003
It was fury, and rage, and. . .death.

109
00:06:52,653 --> 00:06:55,330
It was him.

110
00:06:55,370 --> 00:06:57,687
It was the Devil.

111
00:06:57,727 --> 00:07:00,349
Come on.

112
00:07:05,958 --> 00:07:09,472
What's Strategy Nine?
Open the airlocks.

113
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:15,266
We'll be safe inside the lockdown.
The Ood will get thrown out,
into the vacuum.

114
00:07:15,306 --> 00:07:17,666
So we're going back to a slaughter.

115
00:07:17,706 --> 00:07:19,509
The Devil's work.

116
00:07:20,902 --> 00:07:24,338
COMMUNICATOR HISSES
'OK, we're in. Bring us up. '

117
00:07:24,378 --> 00:07:30,322
Ascension, in three, two, one.

118
00:07:36,323 --> 00:07:39,283
'This is the darkness. '

119
00:07:39,323 --> 00:07:41,079
This is my domain.

120
00:07:41,119 --> 00:07:45,478
You little things
that live in the light,

121
00:07:45,518 --> 00:07:48,234
clinging to your feeble suns,

122
00:07:48,274 --> 00:07:50,670
which die, in the end. . .

123
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:53,668
That's not the Ood.
Something is talking through them.

124
00:07:53,708 --> 00:07:56,465
Only the darkness remains.

125
00:07:56,505 --> 00:08:00,540
This is Captain Zachary Cross Flane,
of Sanctuary Base Six,

126
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:05,416
representing the Torchwood Archive.
You will identify yourself.

127
00:08:05,456 --> 00:08:07,453
You know my name.

128
00:08:07,493 --> 00:08:08,973
What do you want?

129
00:08:09,013 --> 00:08:11,810
You will die here. All of you.

130
00:08:11,850 --> 00:08:14,085
This planet is your grave.

131
00:08:14,125 --> 00:08:16,483
It's him. It's him. It's him.

132
00:08:16,523 --> 00:08:19,719
If you are the Beast,
then answer me this. Which one?

133
00:08:19,759 --> 00:08:22,876
Cos the universe has been busy
since you've been gone.

134
00:08:22,916 --> 00:08:25,393
There's more religions
than there are planets.

135
00:08:25,433 --> 00:08:29,866
The Arkiphets, Quoldonity,
Christianity, Pash-Pash,

136
00:08:29,906 --> 00:08:33,706
New Judaism, San Claar,
the Church of the Tin Vagabond. . .

137
00:08:33,746 --> 00:08:35,825
Which Devil are you? All of them.

138
00:08:35,865 --> 00:08:39,300
What, then you're the truth
behind the myth(? )

139
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:41,259
This one knows me.

140
00:08:41,299 --> 00:08:46,253
As I know him.
The killer of his own kind.

141
00:08:47,333 --> 00:08:49,287
How did you end up on this rock?

142
00:08:49,327 --> 00:08:53,125
The Disciples of the Light
rose up against me,

143
00:08:53,165 --> 00:08:56,762
and chained me in the Pit
for all eternity.

144
00:08:56,802 --> 00:08:59,879
When was this? Before time.

145
00:08:59,919 --> 00:09:03,434
What does that mean? Before time.

146
00:09:03,474 --> 00:09:05,273
What does "before time" MEAN?

147
00:09:05,313 --> 00:09:10,070
Before time and light
and space and matter.

148
00:09:10,110 --> 00:09:12,786
Before the cataclysm.

149
00:09:12,826 --> 00:09:16,185
Before this universe was created.

150
00:09:16,225 --> 00:09:19,260
That's impossible. No life
could have existed back then.

151
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:22,252
Is that your religion?

152
00:09:23,455 --> 00:09:26,933
It's a belief. You know nothing.

153
00:09:26,973 --> 00:09:29,687
All of you, so small.

154
00:09:29,727 --> 00:09:33,682
The Captain, so scared of command.

155
00:09:33,722 --> 00:09:39,078
The soldier,
haunted by the eyes of his wife.

156
00:09:39,118 --> 00:09:43,993
The scientist,
still running from Daddy.

157
00:09:44,033 --> 00:09:47,270
The little boy who lied.

158
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:49,547
The virgin.

159
00:09:49,587 --> 00:09:51,945
And the lost girl.

160
00:09:51,985 --> 00:09:55,063
So far away from home.

161
00:09:55,103 --> 00:10:01,055
The valiant child
who will die in battle, so very soon.

162
00:10:01,095 --> 00:10:03,135
Doctor, what does that mean?

163
00:10:03,175 --> 00:10:05,488
Rose, don't listen.
What does it mean? !

164
00:10:05,528 --> 00:10:08,365
You will die. . .

165
00:10:08,405 --> 00:10:11,107
. .and I will live.

166
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,040
What the hell was that?

167
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:17,837
I had that thing inside my head!

168
00:10:17,877 --> 00:10:19,914
Doctor, what did it mean?

169
00:10:19,954 --> 00:10:23,511
What do we do? Jefferson, Zack,
what do we do? Captain. . . ?

170
00:10:23,551 --> 00:10:27,347
The orbit, the planet,
the black hole - everything's true.

171
00:10:27,387 --> 00:10:29,466
How did it know that?
Did anyone. . . ?

172
00:10:29,506 --> 00:10:33,562
What battle? What did it mean? Stop!
What do we do?

173
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:37,018
FEEDBACK WHINES

174
00:10:37,058 --> 00:10:40,970
If you want voices in the dark,
listen to mine.
It's playing on basic fears.

175
00:10:41,010 --> 00:10:46,925
Darkness, childhood, nightmares,
all that stuff. But that's how the
Devil works. Or a good psychologist.

176
00:10:46,965 --> 00:10:49,243
How did it know about my father?

177
00:10:49,283 --> 00:10:52,840
OK. But what makes his version
of the truth any better than mine?

178
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:56,322
Cos I'll tell you what I can see.
Humans. Brilliant humans.

179
00:10:56,362 --> 00:11:00,154
Humans who travelled
all the way across space,
flying in a tiny rocket,

180
00:11:00,194 --> 00:11:03,789
into the orbit of a black hole,
just for the sake of discovery!

181
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:06,788
That's amazing! D'you hear me?
Amazing.

182
00:11:06,828 --> 00:11:09,546
All of you. The captain.
His officer. His elder.

183
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:11,302
His juniors. His friends.

184
00:11:11,342 --> 00:11:15,936
All with one advantage.
The Beast is alone. We are not.

185
00:11:15,976 --> 00:11:18,393
If we can use that
to fight against him. . .

186
00:11:23,007 --> 00:11:25,306
The cable snapped! Get out!

187
00:11:32,999 --> 00:11:35,356
Doctor, we lost the cable!

188
00:11:35,396 --> 00:11:38,234
Doctor, are you all right? Doctor?

189
00:11:38,274 --> 00:11:40,512
Comms are down.
(Doctor, can you hear me? )

190
00:11:40,552 --> 00:11:43,708
I've still got life-signs,
but. . .we've lost the capsule.

191
00:11:43,748 --> 00:11:46,265
There's no way out.

192
00:11:46,305 --> 00:11:48,108
They're stuck down there.

193
00:11:52,659 --> 00:11:54,732
How much air have we got?

194
00:11:54,772 --> 00:11:57,973
60 minutes.

195
00:11:58,013 --> 00:11:59,611
55.

196
00:12:00,810 --> 00:12:02,648
But we've got to bring them back!

197
00:12:02,688 --> 00:12:06,084
They're ten miles down. We haven't
got another ten miles of cable.

198
00:12:06,124 --> 00:12:09,690
EXPLOSION
Captain?

199
00:12:10,759 --> 00:12:12,435
Situation report.

200
00:12:12,475 --> 00:12:16,531
BANGING

201
00:12:26,184 --> 00:12:27,902
It's the Ood.

202
00:12:27,942 --> 00:12:31,379
They're cutting through
the door-bolts, they're breaking in.

203
00:12:31,419 --> 00:12:34,253
Yes, same on Door 25.
How long's it gonna take?

204
00:12:34,293 --> 00:12:38,064
Well, it's only a basic frame,
should take ten minutes.

205
00:12:39,408 --> 00:12:40,932
Eight.

206
00:12:42,405 --> 00:12:45,204
I've got a security frame -
it might last a bit longer.

207
00:12:45,244 --> 00:12:49,678
But that doesn't help you.
Right. So! We've got to stop them,
or get out, or both.

208
00:12:49,718 --> 00:12:52,195
I'll take both, yeah, but how? !

209
00:12:52,235 --> 00:12:55,317
You heard the Doctor. Why d'you
think that thing cut him off?

210
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:59,189
Cos he was making sense,
he was telling you to think
your way out of this!

211
00:12:59,229 --> 00:13:01,507
Come on! For starters,
we need some light.

212
00:13:01,547 --> 00:13:05,823
Zack, there's got to be
some sort of power, somewhere.
There's nothing I can do.

213
00:13:05,863 --> 00:13:08,660
Some Captain!
Stuck in here, pressing buttons.

214
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:13,452
But that's what the Doctor meant!
Press the right buttons!
They've gutted the generators!

215
00:13:13,492 --> 00:13:17,089
But. . .the rocket's
got an independent supply.

216
00:13:17,129 --> 00:13:19,487
If I can reroute that. . .

217
00:13:19,527 --> 00:13:22,564
Mr Jefferson!
Open the bypass conduits,

218
00:13:22,604 --> 00:13:24,961
override the safety.

219
00:13:25,001 --> 00:13:28,361
Opening bypass conduits, sir!

220
00:13:28,401 --> 00:13:31,395
Channeling rocket feed.

221
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:36,471
In three, two, one.

222
00:13:36,511 --> 00:13:39,273
Power!

223
00:13:39,313 --> 00:13:42,945
There we go! Let there be light!
What about that Strategy Nine thing?

224
00:13:42,985 --> 00:13:45,103
Not enough power - needs 100%.

225
00:13:45,143 --> 00:13:48,775
Right. We need a way out. Zack,
Mr Jefferson, start working on that.

226
00:13:48,815 --> 00:13:51,174
Toby, what about you?
I'm not a soldier!

227
00:13:51,214 --> 00:13:54,448
No, you're the archaeologist.
What do you know about the Pit?

228
00:13:54,488 --> 00:13:58,169
We can't even translate the language,
but. . . Hold on. Maybe. . .

229
00:13:58,209 --> 00:14:00,325
What is it?

230
00:14:00,365 --> 00:14:04,759
Since that thing was inside my head,
the letters make more sense.

231
00:14:04,799 --> 00:14:09,476
Then get to work. Anything
you can translate, just. . .anything.

232
00:14:09,516 --> 00:14:13,430
As for you, Danny boy,
you're in charge of the Ood.
Any way of stopping them?

233
00:14:13,470 --> 00:14:15,589
Well. . . I don't know.

234
00:14:15,629 --> 00:14:17,788
Then find out!

235
00:14:17,828 --> 00:14:23,112
Sooner we get control of this base,
the sooner we can get the
Doctor out. Now get going. Shift!

236
00:14:28,417 --> 00:14:32,531
We've got all this cable,
might as well use it.

237
00:14:32,571 --> 00:14:37,325
The drum's disconnected,
we could adapt it. Feed it through. . .

238
00:14:37,365 --> 00:14:39,562
And then what?

239
00:14:39,602 --> 00:14:41,442
Abseil.

240
00:14:41,482 --> 00:14:43,558
Into the Pit.

241
00:14:43,598 --> 00:14:45,316
Abseil! Right!

242
00:14:45,356 --> 00:14:49,036
We're running out of air, with no way
back. It's the only thing we CAN do.

243
00:14:49,076 --> 00:14:52,470
Even if it's the last thing
we ever achieve.

244
00:14:52,510 --> 00:14:55,107
I'll get back. Rose is up there.

245
00:14:55,147 --> 00:15:00,064
Then maybe the key to that
is finding out what's in the Pit.

246
00:15:00,104 --> 00:15:03,417
Well. It's half of a good plan.

247
00:15:03,457 --> 00:15:05,217
What's the other half?

248
00:15:05,257 --> 00:15:08,084
I go down. Not you.

249
00:15:09,570 --> 00:15:14,076
Junctions 5, 6, 7. . .

250
00:15:16,365 --> 00:15:19,027
Re-route filters 16 to 24. Go.

251
00:15:21,043 --> 00:15:24,118
There's all sorts of viruses
that could stop the Ood.

252
00:15:24,158 --> 00:15:26,955
Trouble is,
we haven't got them on board.

253
00:15:26,995 --> 00:15:29,673
Well, that's handy,
listing things we haven't got.

254
00:15:29,713 --> 00:15:32,415
We haven't got a swimming pool
either, or a Tesco.

255
00:15:34,030 --> 00:15:37,500
Oh, my God, it says yes!
I can do it!

256
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:42,018
Hypothetically, if you flip
the monitor, broadcast a flare,

257
00:15:42,058 --> 00:15:45,532
it can disrupt the telepathy.
Brainstorm ! What happens to the Ood?

258
00:15:45,572 --> 00:15:47,332
It'll tank them, spark-out!

259
00:15:47,372 --> 00:15:49,648
There we are then - do it!

260
00:15:49,688 --> 00:15:54,406
No, but I'd have to transmit
from the central monitor.

261
00:15:54,446 --> 00:15:57,648
We need to go to Ood Habitation.

262
00:15:59,321 --> 00:16:01,398
That's what we'll do then.

263
00:16:01,438 --> 00:16:04,915
Mr Jefferson, sir, any way out?

264
00:16:04,955 --> 00:16:07,792
Just about. There's a network
of maintenance tunnels

265
00:16:07,832 --> 00:16:10,350
running underneath the base.

266
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:14,584
Ventilation shafts!
I appreciate the reference,
but there's no ventilation.

267
00:16:14,624 --> 00:16:19,058
No air, in fact - they were designed
for machines, not lifeforms.

268
00:16:19,098 --> 00:16:22,974
But I can manipulate
the oxygen field from here,

269
00:16:23,014 --> 00:16:25,293
create discrete pockets
of atmosphere.

270
00:16:25,333 --> 00:16:29,329
If I control it manually, I can
follow you through the network.

271
00:16:29,369 --> 00:16:33,963
Right! So. . . We go down, and
you make the air follow us? By hand?

272
00:16:34,003 --> 00:16:37,123
You wanted me pressing buttons.
Yep. I asked for it. OK.

273
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:39,705
We need to get to Ood Habitation.
Work out a route.

274
00:16:41,757 --> 00:16:43,713
That should hold it.

275
00:16:43,753 --> 00:16:47,072
How's it going? Fine. Should work.

276
00:16:47,112 --> 00:16:49,905
Doesn't feel like
such a good idea now.

277
00:16:52,422 --> 00:16:55,620
There it is again. That itch.

278
00:16:55,660 --> 00:16:57,936
Go down, go down,
go down, go down. . .

279
00:16:57,976 --> 00:17:02,573
The urge to jump. D'you know where
it comes from, that sensation?

280
00:17:02,613 --> 00:17:07,328
Genetic heritage, ever since
we were primates in the trees.

281
00:17:07,368 --> 00:17:09,806
It's our body's way of testing us,

282
00:17:09,846 --> 00:17:14,162
calculating whether or not
we can reach the next branch.

283
00:17:14,202 --> 00:17:16,440
No, that's not it.

284
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:18,398
That's too kind.

285
00:17:18,438 --> 00:17:22,157
It's not the urge to jump,
it's deeper than that.

286
00:17:22,197 --> 00:17:23,913
It's the urge to fall.

287
00:17:23,953 --> 00:17:26,780
Doctor!

288
00:17:28,190 --> 00:17:30,665
You OK? Not bad, thanks.

289
00:17:30,705 --> 00:17:35,019
Wall of the Pit seems to be
the same as the cavern,

290
00:17:35,059 --> 00:17:37,336
just. . . not much of it.

291
00:17:37,376 --> 00:17:42,296
There's a crust about 20ft down,
and then. . .

292
00:17:43,691 --> 00:17:45,784
Nothing. Just the Pit.

293
00:17:47,128 --> 00:17:49,725
OK, then. Lower me down.

294
00:17:49,765 --> 00:17:51,374
Here we go, then.

295
00:17:59,555 --> 00:18:02,792
Danny! Hold on, just conforming.

296
00:18:02,832 --> 00:18:05,910
Danny, we've got to go now! Come on!

297
00:18:06,950 --> 00:18:11,061
There! Put that into the monitor
and it's a bad time to be an Ood!

298
00:18:11,101 --> 00:18:12,579
We're coming back, got that?

299
00:18:12,619 --> 00:18:15,259
We're coming back
and getting the Doctor out.

300
00:18:15,299 --> 00:18:18,776
OK, Danny, you go first, then you,
then Toby. I'll go last.

301
00:18:18,816 --> 00:18:20,619
Now come on, quick as you can.

302
00:18:24,371 --> 00:18:28,207
God, it stinks. You all right?
Yeah, laughing( !)

303
00:18:28,247 --> 00:18:32,098
Which way do we go? Just go straight
ahead, keep going till I say so.

304
00:18:39,155 --> 00:18:42,587
Not your best angle, Danny. Oi.
Stop it!

305
00:18:42,627 --> 00:18:44,885
I dunno, could be worse. Oi!

306
00:18:45,867 --> 00:18:49,223
Straight on till you find
Junction 7.1. Keep breathing.

307
00:18:49,263 --> 00:18:52,829
I'm feeding you air. I've got you.

308
00:19:06,206 --> 00:19:08,483
We're at 7.1, sir.

309
00:19:08,523 --> 00:19:10,337
OK, I've got you.

310
00:19:12,921 --> 00:19:15,277
I'm just aerating the next section.

311
00:19:15,317 --> 00:19:18,474
Getting kinda cramped, sir.
Can't you hurry it up?

312
00:19:18,514 --> 00:19:21,270
I'm working on half-power here.
Stop complaining.

313
00:19:21,310 --> 00:19:24,186
Mr Jefferson said, stop complaining.
I heard. He heard.

314
00:19:24,226 --> 00:19:27,747
The air's getting a bit thin.
HE's complaining now. I heard.

315
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:32,977
Danny, is that you?
I'm not exactly happy!

316
00:19:33,017 --> 00:19:36,412
I'm just moving the air, I've got
to oxygenate the next section.

317
00:19:36,452 --> 00:19:39,491
Now, keep calm,
or it's gonna feel worse.

318
00:19:39,531 --> 00:19:41,743
CLATTER

319
00:19:42,928 --> 00:19:46,286
What was that? Mr Jefferson,
what was that? What was that noise?

320
00:19:46,326 --> 00:19:48,402
Captain. What was that?

321
00:19:48,442 --> 00:19:53,156
The junction in Habitation Five's
been opened. It must be the Ood.

322
00:19:53,196 --> 00:19:57,750
They're in the tunnels.
Well, open the gate! I've got to
get the air in! Just open it, sir!

323
00:19:57,790 --> 00:20:01,188
Where are they, are they close?
I can't tell, I can't see them.

324
00:20:01,228 --> 00:20:04,146
The computer doesn't register Ood
as proper lifeforms.

325
00:20:04,186 --> 00:20:06,853
Whose idea was that? ! Open the GATE!

326
00:20:10,896 --> 00:20:13,558
Danny, turn left, immediate left!

327
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:20,728
The Ood, sir - can't you trap them,
cut off the air?

328
00:20:20,768 --> 00:20:23,674
Not without cutting off yours.

329
00:20:27,319 --> 00:20:31,995
Danny, turn right, go right. . .
Go faster, they're gonna catch up!

330
00:20:32,035 --> 00:20:36,070
I'll maintain defensive position.
You can't stop!

331
00:20:36,110 --> 00:20:40,105
Miss Tyler, that's my job. You've
got your task - now see to it!

332
00:20:40,145 --> 00:20:42,812
You heard what he said, now shift!

333
00:20:59,051 --> 00:21:01,885
8.2. Open 8.2.

334
00:21:01,925 --> 00:21:04,362
Zack, open 8.2!

335
00:21:04,402 --> 00:21:06,879
I've got to aerate it. Open it NOW!

336
00:21:06,919 --> 00:21:10,079
I'm TRYING!

337
00:21:10,119 --> 00:21:12,232
Danny, stop it, that's not helping!

338
00:21:12,272 --> 00:21:14,309
Zack! Get it open!

339
00:21:14,349 --> 00:21:18,106
Jefferson, I've got to open 8.2
by closing 8.1.

340
00:21:18,146 --> 00:21:21,822
You've got to get past the junction!
Now, move!

341
00:21:21,862 --> 00:21:24,575
That's an order! Now, move!

342
00:21:27,859 --> 00:21:32,284
I'm gonna lose oxygen, Jefferson,
I can't stop the automatics!

343
00:21:35,090 --> 00:21:37,567
That's it, come on, come on!

344
00:21:37,607 --> 00:21:40,644
Danny, turn left.
Head for 9.2, that's the last one.

345
00:21:40,684 --> 00:21:43,601
Jefferson,
you've got to move faster!

346
00:21:43,641 --> 00:21:46,558
John! Move! MOVE! Mr Jefferson!

347
00:21:46,598 --> 00:21:49,425
Come on! KEEP GOING!

348
00:21:53,188 --> 00:21:55,467
'Regret to inform you, sir.

349
00:21:55,507 --> 00:21:57,664
'I was a bit slow.

350
00:21:57,704 --> 00:22:00,063
'Not so fast, these days. '

351
00:22:00,103 --> 00:22:02,501
I can't open 8.1, John.

352
00:22:02,541 --> 00:22:05,058
Not without losing
air for the others.

353
00:22:05,098 --> 00:22:06,935
And quite right too, sir.

354
00:22:06,975 --> 00:22:09,233
I think I bought them a little time.

355
00:22:11,052 --> 00:22:13,570
'There's nothing I can do, John. '

356
00:22:13,610 --> 00:22:15,646
I'm sorry.

357
00:22:15,686 --> 00:22:19,843
You've done enough, sir.
Made a very good captain,
under the circumstances.

358
00:22:19,883 --> 00:22:24,760
Might I ask, if you can't
add oxygen to this section,

359
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:28,350
can you speed up the
process of its removal?

360
00:22:28,390 --> 00:22:30,989
I don't understand. What d'you mean?

361
00:22:31,029 --> 00:22:34,505
Well, if I might choose
the manner of my departure, sir,

362
00:22:34,545 --> 00:22:37,662
lack of air
seems more natural than. . .

363
00:22:37,702 --> 00:22:43,376
Well, let's say, death by Ood.

364
00:22:43,416 --> 00:22:46,174
I'd appreciate it, sir.

365
00:22:46,214 --> 00:22:48,453
Godspeed, Mr Jefferson.

366
00:22:48,493 --> 00:22:51,206
Thank you, sir.

367
00:23:00,282 --> 00:23:05,473
Report.
Officer John Maynard Jefferson, PKD

368
00:23:05,513 --> 00:23:09,668
deceased, with honours,

369
00:23:09,708 --> 00:23:13,228
43K 2.1.

370
00:23:13,268 --> 00:23:15,106
Zack.

371
00:23:15,146 --> 00:23:17,622
We're at the final junction.

372
00:23:17,662 --> 00:23:20,939
9.2.

373
00:23:20,979 --> 00:23:23,136
And, uh. . .

374
00:23:23,176 --> 00:23:26,814
If my respects could be on record,
he saved our lives.

375
00:23:26,854 --> 00:23:31,478
Noted. Opening 9.2.

376
00:23:34,085 --> 00:23:37,601
Lower 9.2! Zack, LOWER IT!
Back back back!

377
00:23:37,641 --> 00:23:41,287
We can't go back, 8.2's sealed off -
we're stuck!

378
00:23:42,316 --> 00:23:44,739
Come on! UP!

379
00:23:51,545 --> 00:23:53,718
Come on! Toby, come ON !

380
00:23:56,102 --> 00:23:57,739
Toby, get out of there!

381
00:23:57,779 --> 00:24:00,446
Help me! Oh, my God, help me!

382
00:24:05,653 --> 00:24:07,826
It's this way!

383
00:24:17,357 --> 00:24:20,034
EXPLOSION

384
00:24:20,074 --> 00:24:22,332
Hurry it up!

385
00:24:24,472 --> 00:24:26,716
Get it in. Danny, get it done.

386
00:24:26,756 --> 00:24:29,826
Transmit! I'm trying, I'm trying.
I'm getting it in. . .

387
00:24:29,866 --> 00:24:31,270
Stop them !

388
00:24:37,338 --> 00:24:40,205
Danny, get that thing transmitting!

389
00:24:42,975 --> 00:24:45,921
ELECTRONIC SCREECH

390
00:25:01,595 --> 00:25:04,190
You did it! We did it!

391
00:25:04,230 --> 00:25:06,329
Yes! Oh, yes!

392
00:25:08,786 --> 00:25:12,103
Zack, we did it, the Ood are down!
Now we've got to get the Doctor.

393
00:25:12,143 --> 00:25:13,946
On my way!

394
00:25:15,257 --> 00:25:18,937
You get representations of the
horned beast across the universe,

395
00:25:18,977 --> 00:25:21,425
in the myths and legends
of a million worlds.

396
00:25:21,465 --> 00:25:26,368
Earth, Draconia,
Vel Consadine, Daemos,

397
00:25:26,408 --> 00:25:29,646
the Kaled God of War. . . The same
image, over and over again.

398
00:25:29,686 --> 00:25:33,080
Maybe that idea came from somewhere.

399
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:35,556
Bleeding through.

400
00:25:35,596 --> 00:25:38,674
A thought at the back
of every sentient mind.

401
00:25:38,714 --> 00:25:40,510
Emanating from here?

402
00:25:40,550 --> 00:25:43,829
Could be. If this is the original. . .

403
00:25:43,869 --> 00:25:49,582
does that make it real, does that
make it the actual Devil, though?

404
00:25:49,622 --> 00:25:51,980
Well, if that's
what you want to believe.

405
00:25:52,020 --> 00:25:55,256
Maybe that's what the Devil is,
in the end. An idea.

406
00:25:58,106 --> 00:26:00,053
That's it.

407
00:26:00,093 --> 00:26:03,171
That's all we've got.

408
00:26:03,211 --> 00:26:05,808
You getting any sort of readout?

409
00:26:05,848 --> 00:26:07,802
Nothing.

410
00:26:07,842 --> 00:26:09,719
Could be miles to go.

411
00:26:09,759 --> 00:26:15,009
Or, could be 30 feet,
there's no way of telling.

412
00:26:17,194 --> 00:26:19,391
I could survive 30 feet.

413
00:26:19,431 --> 00:26:21,723
Oh, no, you don't,
I'm pulling you back up.

414
00:26:25,027 --> 00:26:26,954
What are you doing? !

415
00:26:26,994 --> 00:26:30,539
You bring me back, and we're just
gonna sit there and run out of air.

416
00:26:30,579 --> 00:26:32,587
I've got to go down.

417
00:26:32,627 --> 00:26:35,456
But you can't. Doctor, you can't!

418
00:26:35,496 --> 00:26:37,583
Call it an act of faith.

419
00:26:40,170 --> 00:26:42,811
I don't want to die on my own.

420
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:45,769
I know.

421
00:26:50,079 --> 00:26:51,877
Doctor, are you there?

422
00:26:51,917 --> 00:26:54,036
Doctor? Ida? Can you hear me?

423
00:26:54,076 --> 00:26:57,471
The comms are still down. I can
patch them through the central desk

424
00:26:57,511 --> 00:27:00,099
and boost the signal. . .
Just give me a minute.

425
00:27:03,265 --> 00:27:08,461
I didn't ask. Have you got any sort
of faith, or. . . ? Not really.

426
00:27:08,501 --> 00:27:13,536
I was brought up Neo-Classic,
Congregational.

427
00:27:13,576 --> 00:27:15,868
Cos of my mum, she was. . .

428
00:27:19,172 --> 00:27:21,720
My old mum.

429
00:27:22,978 --> 00:27:25,081
But no. I never believed.

430
00:27:25,121 --> 00:27:27,130
Neo-Classics, have they got a devil?

431
00:27:27,170 --> 00:27:30,361
No.  Not as such.  Just...

432
00:27:31,475 --> 00:27:33,712
. .the things that men do.

433
00:27:33,752 --> 00:27:36,704
Same thing, in the end.
And what about you?

434
00:27:42,746 --> 00:27:46,621
I believe. . .
I believe I haven't seen everything.

435
00:27:46,661 --> 00:27:48,964
I dunno.

436
00:27:50,667 --> 00:27:52,377
Funny, isn't it?

437
00:27:52,417 --> 00:27:55,172
The things you make up. The rules.

438
00:27:55,212 --> 00:27:58,886
If that thing had said it came from
beyond the universe, I'd believe it,

439
00:27:58,926 --> 00:28:02,049
but before the universe? Impossible.

440
00:28:03,401 --> 00:28:06,108
Doesn't fit my rules.

441
00:28:08,957 --> 00:28:11,289
Still.
Maybe that's why I keep travelling.

442
00:28:13,752 --> 00:28:15,845
To be proved wrong.

443
00:28:19,029 --> 00:28:20,553
Thank you, Ida.

444
00:28:20,593 --> 00:28:23,503
Don't go!

445
00:28:23,543 --> 00:28:25,539
If they get back in touch. . .

446
00:28:25,579 --> 00:28:29,225
If you talk to Rose,
just tell her. . .

447
00:28:36,288 --> 00:28:38,381
Tell her. . .

448
00:28:41,603 --> 00:28:43,901
Oh, she knows.

449
00:28:46,957 --> 00:28:48,675
'Doctor? Are you there?

450
00:28:48,715 --> 00:28:51,562
'Doctor? Ida? Can you hear me?'

451
00:28:51,602 --> 00:28:54,338
Are you there, Doctor? He's gone.

452
00:28:56,148 --> 00:28:58,186
What d'you mean, he's gone?

453
00:28:58,226 --> 00:29:00,105
He fell.

454
00:29:00,145 --> 00:29:02,528
Into the Pit.

455
00:29:03,582 --> 00:29:06,339
I don't know how deep it is.
Miles and miles and miles.

456
00:29:06,379 --> 00:29:08,904
But. . . What d'you mean, he fell?

457
00:29:08,944 --> 00:29:11,316
I couldn't stop him.

458
00:29:14,576 --> 00:29:16,259
He said your name.

459
00:29:22,001 --> 00:29:24,834
I'm sorry.

460
00:29:26,803 --> 00:29:31,551
Ida. . .
There's no way of reaching you.

461
00:29:31,591 --> 00:29:36,189
No cable, no backup,
you're ten miles down.

462
00:29:36,229 --> 00:29:38,144
We can't get there.

463
00:29:38,184 --> 00:29:40,772
You should see this place, Zack.

464
00:29:45,066 --> 00:29:47,523
It's beautiful.

465
00:29:50,050 --> 00:29:53,042
I wanted to discover things,

466
00:29:55,245 --> 00:29:57,090
and here I am.

467
00:29:57,130 --> 00:29:58,681
We've got to abandon the base.

468
00:29:58,721 --> 00:30:01,639
I'm declaring this mission unsafe.

469
00:30:01,679 --> 00:30:05,477
All we can do is make sure
no-one ever comes here again.

470
00:30:05,517 --> 00:30:08,153
But we'll never find out what it was.

471
00:30:08,193 --> 00:30:09,870
Maybe that's best.

472
00:30:09,910 --> 00:30:12,168
Yeah.

473
00:30:15,584 --> 00:30:18,624
Officer Scott. . . It's all right.

474
00:30:18,664 --> 00:30:20,478
Just go.

475
00:30:22,027 --> 00:30:25,906
Good luck. And you.

476
00:30:31,210 --> 00:30:35,963
Danny, Toby,
close down the feed-links,
get the retrotopes online.

477
00:30:36,003 --> 00:30:39,241
Then get to the rocket and strap
yourselves in. We're leaving.

478
00:30:39,281 --> 00:30:42,836
I'm not going.
Rose, there's space for you.

479
00:30:42,876 --> 00:30:45,481
No, I'm gonna wait for the Doctor.

480
00:30:45,521 --> 00:30:47,210
Just like he'd wait for me.

481
00:30:48,870 --> 00:30:52,506
I'm sorry, but. . . he's dead.

482
00:30:52,546 --> 00:30:54,664
You don't know him.

483
00:30:54,704 --> 00:30:57,132
Cos he's not.

484
00:30:59,340 --> 00:31:01,497
I'm telling you, he's not. . .

485
00:31:01,537 --> 00:31:04,132
And even if he was,
how could I leave him?

486
00:31:04,172 --> 00:31:10,025
All on his own, all the way
down there? No, I'm gonna stay.

487
00:31:11,606 --> 00:31:14,043
Then. . . I apologise for this.

488
00:31:14,083 --> 00:31:16,120
Danny, Toby, make her secure.

489
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:18,879
No! No! No! Stop! STOP!

490
00:31:18,919 --> 00:31:21,962
Let me go! GET OFF ME!
I'm not leaving!

491
00:31:25,116 --> 00:31:27,196
I've lost too many people.

492
00:31:27,236 --> 00:31:29,939
I'm not leaving you behind.

493
00:31:31,189 --> 00:31:33,862
Let's get her on board.

494
00:31:37,184 --> 00:31:38,946
Did that one just move?

495
00:31:38,986 --> 00:31:42,015
It's the telepathic field,
it's reasserting itself!

496
00:31:42,055 --> 00:31:43,937
Move it, get to the rocket, move!

497
00:31:51,851 --> 00:31:54,058
Ughhh. . .

498
00:32:03,319 --> 00:32:05,856
I'm breathing!

499
00:32:12,185 --> 00:32:14,483
Air cushion to support the fall.

500
00:32:15,502 --> 00:32:18,416
You can breathe down here, Ida!

501
00:32:18,456 --> 00:32:20,176
Can you hear me, Ida?

502
00:32:20,216 --> 00:32:24,851
Dislocating B clamp, C clamp.
raising blu-nitro to maximum.
How's the negapact feed line?

503
00:32:24,891 --> 00:32:28,445
Clear, ready to go, sir. Oh, for
God's sake, get us out of here!

504
00:32:28,485 --> 00:32:31,802
Captain. Think we're gonna have
a problem. Keep an eye on her.

505
00:32:31,842 --> 00:32:35,279
What did you. . . ?
It's all right, Rose, we're safe.

506
00:32:35,319 --> 00:32:40,808
I'm not going anywhere! Get me
out of this thing. . . Get me OUT!
Aaaaand, lift off!

507
00:32:42,911 --> 00:32:46,074
THEY CHEER

508
00:32:55,016 --> 00:32:57,109
The rocket!

509
00:33:03,330 --> 00:33:06,047
Take me back to the planet.

510
00:33:06,087 --> 00:33:08,484
Take me back! Or what?

511
00:33:08,524 --> 00:33:10,577
Or I'll shoot.

512
00:33:13,038 --> 00:33:15,121
Would you, though?

513
00:33:15,161 --> 00:33:19,137
Would you really?
Is that what your Doctor would want?

514
00:33:25,547 --> 00:33:28,505
I'm sorry. But it's too late,
anyway. Take a look outside.

515
00:33:28,545 --> 00:33:31,142
We can't turn back.

516
00:33:31,182 --> 00:33:35,033
And this is what the Doctor
would have wanted, isn't that right?

517
00:33:40,135 --> 00:33:43,566
History of some big battle. . .
Man against Beast.

518
00:33:43,606 --> 00:33:45,964
Dunno if you're getting this, Ida.
Hope so.

519
00:33:46,004 --> 00:33:49,934
Anyway, they defeated the Beast,
and imprisoned it.

520
00:33:58,079 --> 00:34:00,286
And maybe that's the key.

521
00:34:07,784 --> 00:34:10,537
Or the gate, or the bars, or. . .

522
00:34:10,577 --> 00:34:13,609
DEEP RUMBLING

523
00:34:24,725 --> 00:34:27,842
BEAST GROWLS

524
00:34:33,637 --> 00:34:37,275
What's the joke? Just. . . We made it!

525
00:34:37,315 --> 00:34:39,594
We escaped! We actually did it!

526
00:34:39,634 --> 00:34:41,949
Not all of us.
We're not out of it yet.

527
00:34:41,989 --> 00:34:46,059
we're still the first people
in history to fly away
from a black hole.

528
00:34:46,099 --> 00:34:47,859
Toby, read me the stats.

529
00:34:47,899 --> 00:34:50,017
Gravity funnel holding, sir.

530
00:34:50,057 --> 00:34:51,694
Ohh, it's holding!

531
00:34:51,734 --> 00:34:53,894
I accept that you exist.

532
00:34:53,934 --> 00:34:59,168
I don't have to accept what you are,
but your physical existence,
I give you that.

533
00:34:59,208 --> 00:35:01,605
GROWLING

534
00:35:01,645 --> 00:35:05,483
I don't understand.
I was expected down here.

535
00:35:05,523 --> 00:35:09,516
I was given a safe landing, and air.
GRUNT

536
00:35:09,556 --> 00:35:11,973
You need me for something -
what for?

537
00:35:17,032 --> 00:35:19,349
Have I got to. . . ?

538
00:35:19,389 --> 00:35:21,309
I don't know, beg an audience,
or. . . ?

539
00:35:21,349 --> 00:35:23,305
Is there a ritual?

540
00:35:23,345 --> 00:35:26,540
Some sort of incantation
or summons or spell?

541
00:35:26,580 --> 00:35:29,373
All those things I don't believe in,
are they real?

542
00:35:30,694 --> 00:35:33,527
Speak to me! Tell me!

543
00:35:36,731 --> 00:35:39,048
You won't talk.

544
00:35:39,088 --> 00:35:41,884
Or. . .you can't talk.

545
00:35:41,924 --> 00:35:44,561
BEAST ROARS

546
00:35:44,601 --> 00:35:48,556
Hold on, hold on, wait a minute,
just let me. . .

547
00:35:48,596 --> 00:35:50,156
Oh! No.

548
00:35:50,196 --> 00:35:52,073
Yes! No.

549
00:35:52,113 --> 00:35:55,870
Think it through! You spoke
before, I heard your voice.

550
00:35:55,910 --> 00:35:59,431
An intelligent voice.
No, more than that, brilliant.

551
00:36:01,221 --> 00:36:05,858
But looking at you now,
all I can see. . .

552
00:36:05,898 --> 00:36:08,455
BEAST ROARS

553
00:36:08,495 --> 00:36:12,292
. . is the Beast.

554
00:36:12,332 --> 00:36:14,249
The animal.

555
00:36:14,289 --> 00:36:16,408
Just. . .the body.

556
00:36:16,448 --> 00:36:20,446
You're just the body, the physical
form. What happened to your mind?

557
00:36:20,486 --> 00:36:22,841
Hmm?

558
00:36:22,881 --> 00:36:26,163
Were's it gone?
Where's that intelligence?

559
00:36:29,636 --> 00:36:31,763
Oh no. . .

560
00:36:33,394 --> 00:36:38,303
Stats at 53, funnel stable at 66.5,
hull pressure constant.

561
00:36:38,343 --> 00:36:41,661
Smooth as we can, sir,
all the way back home.

562
00:36:41,701 --> 00:36:43,788
Co-ordinates set for Planet Earth.

563
00:36:45,375 --> 00:36:48,208
You're imprisoned, long time ago.

564
00:36:49,255 --> 00:36:52,928
Before the universe, after,
sideways, in between,
doesn't matter.

565
00:36:52,968 --> 00:36:55,526
And the prison is perfect.

566
00:36:55,566 --> 00:36:58,163
It's absolute, it's eternal. . .

567
00:36:58,203 --> 00:36:59,883
Oh, yes.

568
00:36:59,923 --> 00:37:03,797
Open the prison,
and the gravity field collapses,

569
00:37:03,837 --> 00:37:07,289
this planet
falls into the black hole.

570
00:37:08,317 --> 00:37:10,632
You escape, you die. Brilliant!

571
00:37:10,672 --> 00:37:12,750
But that's just the body.

572
00:37:12,790 --> 00:37:15,457
The body's trapped, that's all.

573
00:37:16,983 --> 00:37:21,454
The Devil is an idea, in all
those civilisations, just an idea.

574
00:37:22,617 --> 00:37:25,335
But an idea is hard to kill.

575
00:37:25,375 --> 00:37:27,963
An idea can escape!

576
00:37:29,413 --> 00:37:35,006
The mind, the mind of the great
Beast, the mind can escape.

577
00:37:35,046 --> 00:37:37,683
Oh, but that's it!

578
00:37:37,723 --> 00:37:39,840
You didn't give me air.
Your jailers did!

579
00:37:39,880 --> 00:37:43,160
They set this up,
all those years ago.

580
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:45,838
They need me alive!

581
00:37:45,878 --> 00:37:49,155
Because if you're escaping
then I've got to stop you.

582
00:37:49,195 --> 00:37:51,532
BEAST ROARS

583
00:37:54,466 --> 00:37:57,462
If I destroy your prison,
your body is destroyed.

584
00:37:57,502 --> 00:37:59,794
Your mind with it?

585
00:38:07,491 --> 00:38:11,329
But then you're clever enough to
use this whole system against me.

586
00:38:11,369 --> 00:38:16,084
If I destroy this planet,
then I destroy the gravity field.

587
00:38:17,003 --> 00:38:20,881
The rocket.
The rocket loses protection.

588
00:38:20,921 --> 00:38:22,724
Falls into the Black Hole.

589
00:38:25,274 --> 00:38:27,822
I have to sacrifice Rose.

590
00:38:29,193 --> 00:38:31,889
BEAST CACKLES

591
00:38:34,502 --> 00:38:36,899
It doesn't make sense.

592
00:38:36,939 --> 00:38:40,219
We escaped, but there's a thousand
ways it could've killed us.

593
00:38:40,259 --> 00:38:45,850
It could've ripped out the air,
or burnt us, or anything,

594
00:38:45,890 --> 00:38:48,102
But it let us go - why?

595
00:38:49,607 --> 00:38:51,644
Unless it wanted us to escape.

596
00:38:51,684 --> 00:38:54,044
Hey, Rose, do us a favour.

597
00:38:54,084 --> 00:38:55,887
Shut up.

598
00:38:56,881 --> 00:39:01,635
Almost there. We're beyond the
reach of the Black Hole in 40, 39. . .

599
00:39:01,675 --> 00:39:03,593
So that's the trap.

600
00:39:03,633 --> 00:39:06,666
Or the test or the final judgement,
I don't know.

601
00:39:08,428 --> 00:39:10,931
But if I kill you, I kill her.

602
00:39:15,502 --> 00:39:18,259
Except that implies,

603
00:39:18,299 --> 00:39:21,813
in this big, grand scheme
of gods and devils,

604
00:39:21,853 --> 00:39:24,252
she's just a victim.

605
00:39:24,292 --> 00:39:27,010
But I've seen a lot of the universe.

606
00:39:27,050 --> 00:39:30,046
I've seen fake gods, and bad gods,

607
00:39:30,086 --> 00:39:32,084
and demi-gods and would-be gods,

608
00:39:32,124 --> 00:39:36,161
and out of all that,
out of that whole pantheon,

609
00:39:36,201 --> 00:39:38,277
if I believe in one thing,

610
00:39:38,317 --> 00:39:40,654
just one thing. . .

611
00:39:41,675 --> 00:39:44,087
I believe in her.

612
00:39:48,546 --> 00:39:51,224
What was that?
What's he doing? What is he doing? !

613
00:39:51,264 --> 00:39:53,780
We've lost the funnel!
Gravity collapse!

614
00:39:53,820 --> 00:39:55,897
What does that mean?
We can't escape!

615
00:39:55,937 --> 00:39:59,014
We're heading straight
for the black hole!

616
00:40:07,526 --> 00:40:09,365
This is your freedom !

617
00:40:09,405 --> 00:40:12,084
Free to die!

618
00:40:12,124 --> 00:40:15,360
You're going into the black hole,
and I'm riding with you!

619
00:40:20,515 --> 00:40:24,229
It's the planet,
the planet's moving!

620
00:40:24,269 --> 00:40:26,402
It's falling.

621
00:40:27,983 --> 00:40:31,699
I am the rage and the bile
and the ferocity!

622
00:40:31,739 --> 00:40:35,017
I am the prince and the fool
and the agony! It's him, it's Toby!

623
00:40:35,057 --> 00:40:38,975
I am the sin and the fear and the
darkness! The ship's not stable!

624
00:40:39,015 --> 00:40:41,398
What is he? What the hell is he? !

625
00:40:44,649 --> 00:40:46,365
I shall never die!

626
00:40:46,405 --> 00:40:48,125
The thought of me is for ever!

627
00:40:48,165 --> 00:40:52,560
In the bleeding hearts of men, in
their vanity and obsession and lust!

628
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:55,797
Nothing shall ever destroy me!
Nothing!

629
00:40:55,837 --> 00:40:58,095
Go to hell.

630
00:41:08,623 --> 00:41:11,285
Emergency shield!

631
00:41:14,337 --> 00:41:17,374
BEAST HOWLS

632
00:41:19,931 --> 00:41:21,888
We've still lost the gravity funnel.

633
00:41:21,928 --> 00:41:23,609
We can't escape the black hole.

634
00:41:23,649 --> 00:41:26,725
But we stopped him. That's
what the Doctor would have done.

635
00:41:26,765 --> 00:41:30,456
Some victory. We're going in. . .

636
00:41:46,264 --> 00:41:49,461
The planet's lost orbit.
It's falling!

637
00:42:09,042 --> 00:42:12,352
THE DOCTOR LAUGHS

638
00:42:16,030 --> 00:42:18,750
The planet's gone.

639
00:42:18,790 --> 00:42:21,457
I'm sorry. Accelerating.

640
00:42:21,947 --> 00:42:24,584
I did my best.

641
00:42:24,624 --> 00:42:29,417
But hey, first human beings
to fall inside a black hole,

642
00:42:29,457 --> 00:42:31,855
how about that?

643
00:42:31,895 --> 00:42:34,437
History.

644
00:42:45,565 --> 00:42:48,511
What happened?

645
00:42:52,591 --> 00:42:55,429
We're turning.

646
00:42:55,469 --> 00:42:57,190
We're turning around.

647
00:42:57,230 --> 00:42:59,306
We're turning away!

648
00:42:59,346 --> 00:43:01,104
COMMUNICATOR HISSES

649
00:43:01,144 --> 00:43:05,260
'Sorry about the hijack, Captain.
This is the good ship Tardis. '

650
00:43:05,300 --> 00:43:08,338
Now, first things first,
have you got a Rose Tyler on board?

651
00:43:08,378 --> 00:43:10,215
I'm here! It's me!

652
00:43:10,255 --> 00:43:12,416
Oh, my God! Where are you?

653
00:43:12,456 --> 00:43:14,333
I'm just towing you home.

654
00:43:14,373 --> 00:43:17,889
Gravity, shmavity - my people
practically invented black holes.

655
00:43:17,929 --> 00:43:21,006
In fact, they did. Couple of
minutes, we'll be nice and safe.

656
00:43:21,046 --> 00:43:23,443
Oh, and Captain? Can we do a swap?

657
00:43:23,483 --> 00:43:28,515
Say, if you give me Rose Tyler, I'll
give you Ida Scott, how about that?

658
00:43:28,555 --> 00:43:31,752
She's alive? ! Thank God.

659
00:43:31,792 --> 00:43:34,988
Yeah, bit of oxygen starvation,
but she should be all right.

660
00:43:35,028 --> 00:43:37,025
I couldn't save the Ood.

661
00:43:37,065 --> 00:43:39,666
I only had time for one trip.

662
00:43:39,706 --> 00:43:42,063
They went down with the planet.

663
00:43:42,103 --> 00:43:44,379
TARDIS BLEEPS

664
00:43:44,419 --> 00:43:46,219
Entering clear space.

665
00:43:46,259 --> 00:43:48,676
End of the line. Mission closed.

666
00:44:07,593 --> 00:44:11,631
'I don't know, I can't remember. '

667
00:44:11,671 --> 00:44:13,788
Well, it looked like a box!

668
00:44:13,828 --> 00:44:15,586
What d'you mean, a box?

669
00:44:15,626 --> 00:44:19,422
Down in the hold. A big blue box.

670
00:44:19,462 --> 00:44:22,420
It just appeared - I don't know!

671
00:44:22,460 --> 00:44:26,737
'Zack, we'll be off now.
Have a good trip home. '

672
00:44:26,777 --> 00:44:30,093
And the next time
you get curious about something. . .

673
00:44:30,133 --> 00:44:34,088
Oh, what's the point?
You'll just go blundering in.

674
00:44:34,128 --> 00:44:38,244
The human race! But Doctor. . .
what did you find down there?

675
00:44:38,284 --> 00:44:40,479
That creature, what was it?

676
00:44:40,519 --> 00:44:43,796
I don't know.
Never did decipher that writing.

677
00:44:43,836 --> 00:44:47,953
But that's good! Day I know
everything, I might as well stop.

678
00:44:47,993 --> 00:44:50,269
What do you think it was? Really?

679
00:44:50,309 --> 00:44:53,388
I think. . .we beat it.

680
00:44:53,428 --> 00:44:56,869
That's good enough for me. It said
I was going to die in battle.

681
00:44:59,182 --> 00:45:00,865
Then it lied.

682
00:45:02,340 --> 00:45:05,056
Right! Onwards! Upwards! Ida. . .

683
00:45:05,096 --> 00:45:07,414
see you again, maybe. I ope so.

684
00:45:07,454 --> 00:45:09,214
And thanks, boys!

685
00:45:09,254 --> 00:45:13,048
Hang on though, Doctor.
You never really said. . .

686
00:45:13,088 --> 00:45:16,047
You two. . .who are you?

687
00:45:16,087 --> 00:45:19,972
Oh. . .the stuff of legend.

688
00:45:22,875 --> 00:45:27,112
This is the final report
of Sanctuary Base Six.

689
00:45:27,152 --> 00:45:30,269
Officer Tobias Zed.

690
00:45:30,309 --> 00:45:35,624
Deceased, with honours, 43K 2.1.

691
00:45:35,664 --> 00:45:42,258
Also. . . Ood 1 alpha 1, deceased,
with honours.

692
00:45:42,298 --> 00:45:47,834
Ood 1 alpha 2, deceased,
with honours. . .

693
00:45:52,287 --> 00:45:54,124
deceased, with honours,

694
00:45:54,164 --> 00:45:54,704
43K 2.1.

695
00:45:56,364 --> 00:45:57,638
43K 2.1.

696
00:45:57,838 --> 00:46:00,318
I am your salvation.
TARDIS THRUMS

697
00:46:00,358 --> 00:46:04,414
The sound of the universe.
What does it mean?

698
00:46:05,272 --> 00:46:07,310
His name is The Doctor. Doctor what?

699
00:46:07,350 --> 00:46:08,834
Find me that girl!

700
00:46:10,986 --> 00:46:14,143
Here we are, strangers,
and I'm flashing you me knickers!

701
00:46:14,183 --> 00:46:16,460
One step closer
to catching the Doctor.

702
00:46:16,500 --> 00:46:18,678
Don't I know you?
